From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alexandre Derumier <aderumier@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 02:20:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] msrle32: Don't accept a bit depth change for an
 uncompressed frame.

Decompress() copies a BI_RGB frame as is, its size included, but
DecompressQuery() accepted any output depth at least as large as the
input's. The AVI decompressor then used the codec as an RGB24 to RGB32
converter: its 32-bit output samples held the 24-bit frame, with the
24-bit image size, and the downstream filter rejected them
(E_INVALIDARG: the sample shorter than its media type's image).

Game impacted: Gunslinger Stratos 2 (Type X3): autoplugging its movie
graph to an ARGB32 Sample Grabber went WMV decoder, AVI decompressor
(IYUV codec, RGB24), AVI decompressor (msrle32, "RGB32"), Color Space
Converter: no frame reached the grabber.

Reject a depth change for an uncompressed input: autoplug then connects
the RGB24 output to the Color Space Converter directly.
---
--- a/dlls/msrle32/msrle32.c
+++ b/dlls/msrle32/msrle32.c
@@ -1625,6 +1625,9 @@
         hr = ICERR_UNSUPPORTED;
       if (lpbiIn->biBitCount > lpbiOut->biBitCount)
         hr = ICERR_UNSUPPORTED;
+      /* An uncompressed frame is copied as is (Decompress): no depth conversion. */
+      if (lpbiIn->biCompression == BI_RGB && lpbiIn->biBitCount != lpbiOut->biBitCount)
+        hr = ICERR_UNSUPPORTED;
     }
   }
 
